// golden_set.jsonl — shared golden set for Parts A, B, and C.
//
// Format: one JSON object per line. Lines starting with // are ignored by
// the runner (each part's main() must strip them before parsing).
// Build this ONCE, before Part A — the same ~15 questions run against all
// three parts, which is what makes the eval deltas between parts mean
// something instead of being noise from different test data.
//
// Requirements (Module 7's "Build a golden set" slide):
//   ~15 realistic questions, each with expected citations/answers as
//   ground truth. Cover the real branches:
//     - a question that grounds cleanly on the first pass (Part A should
//       already handle these)
//     - a question that should trigger the Critic's revision loop (Part
//       A will fail these; Parts B/C should not)
//     - a general-knowledge question needing no retrieval at all
//
// Schema (per row):
//   {
//     "query": "the user's question",
//     "expected_citations": ["...zero or more expected source references..."],
//     "expects_revision": true | false   // true if this question should
//                                        // trigger at least one Critic
//                                        // reject-and-loop decision
//   }
//
// Example — DELETE this line and add your ~15 entries below.
// {"query": "What authentication methods does the Contoso API support?", "expected_citations": ["docs/auth.md"], "expects_revision": false}
